# Optional — your Floe API key. Without one the server still starts in a
# keyless tier where only get_markets, check_x402_url, and search_floe_docs
# work; every other tool returns a structured AUTH_REQUIRED error. In HTTP
# mode this var is ignored entirely — identity comes from the per-request
# Authorization: Bearer header.
#
# Two key formats are accepted:
#
#   floe_<64-hex>        — Agent key. Identifies one specific agent. Required
#                          for agent-awareness/allowlist tools and x402_pay.
#                          Recommended for spend-side MCP setups. Mint one per
#                          agent via the create_agent_key tool, the dashboard,
#                          or `floe-agent register --name <name>`.
#
#   floe_live_<base62>   — Developer key. Scoped to the developer, not a single
#                          agent. Required for the lifecycle tools (create_agent,
#                          create_agent_key, budgets, funding, webhooks);
#                          agent-awareness tools will 401 with it.
#
# Mint agent keys via the agent setup wizard at https://dev-dashboard.floelabs.xyz
# (or `floe-agent register --name <name>`). Mint developer keys via the
# "API Keys" page at https://dev-dashboard.floelabs.xyz/keys.
FLOE_API_KEY=

# Optional — defaults to https://credit-api.floelabs.xyz
# FLOE_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional — HTTP server port (non-stdio mode only)
# MCP_PORT=3100

# Optional — bind address for HTTP mode (default: 127.0.0.1)
# MCP_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Optional — comma-separated extra origins allowed by CORS in HTTP mode
# MCP_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://myapp.example.com
